  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Two gates for the sound",
      "items": [
        "The facilitator allows Übersetzen (translate:=true, or the setup page's card); off, both workers drop what they were hearing (bridge_node.py 209–218).",
        "The robot's phone may send sound only over this computer's own link (USB, adb reverse) or https (phone_local, wsserver.py 218–223; refused at bridge_node.py 431–436).",
        "The guest phone needs the code from the QR code, new each time Übersetzen is allowed or the setup page asks; a new code drops the guest (bridge_node.py 233–238, wsserver.py 522–526)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Where the words go",
      "items": [
        "To the phones only: talk_send() writes with send_phone() and to the guest, never to a mirror, ROS, a file or the log (bridge_node.py 240–249, wsserver.py 214–217).",
        "An error (nothing heard, no models) goes to the one who spoke only.",
        "The phone that listens says the translation; alone, the robot's phone says it itself (talk.js 127–132)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "What is kept",
      "items": [
        "Nothing: an utterance's sound is dropped when its text is made, at most 30 s of it (translate.py 216–254).",
        "ROS and the setup page get counts: which way, how many words, how long (bridge_node.py 269–273)."
      ]
    }
  ]
